afk: Anthropic multi-account ranking prefers the account whose shared 7d
window resets soonest, plus session-verified identity lookups and
pin-time rate-limit unblocking.

Motivation: Anthropic weekly windows recover on a fixed schedule, so
burning down the account whose 7d window resets soonest wastes the least
quota if it is exhausted. Display paths (status line) also need to name
the account a session is *verifiably* routed to, not the first stored
account the plain lookup falls back to before any getApiKey.

What must survive a rebase:
- `preferEarlierSecondaryReset?: boolean` on CredentialRankingStrategy
  (usage.ts) and the claude strategy opting in (usage/claude.ts).
- `secondaryResetAt` on UsageRankedCandidate (auth/rank.ts), populated at
  BOTH ranking sites in auth/select.ts (#rankApiKeySelections and
  #rankOAuthSelections) via windowResetAt, +Infinity when unknown, so
  unknown resets sort last; orderUsageRankedCandidates carries it onto
  the returned UsageCandidate for the warm-pin eviction check.
- The comparator step sits after the hasPriorityBoost tie-break and
  BEFORE the short-window hot guard (and everything below it), with the
  60s tie tolerance (SECONDARY_RESET_TIE_TOLERANCE_MS) so near-identical
  schedules keep load-balancing.
- The strategy's flag threaded into orderUsageRankedCandidates and both
  compare helpers (rank.ts is a pure module, so the flag is passed, not
  resolved from the provider).
- `oauth.identity(provider, sessionId, { sessionStickyOnly })` (via
  SessionAffinity.activeOAuth): sticky-only lookups suppress the
  pre-attribution fallback to the first stored credential.
- An explicit pin (`sessions.pin` without `restoredAtMs`) clears reactive
  rate-limit blocks on the target (CredentialBlocks.clearAll, wired into
  SessionAffinity) so the next request actually tries it; a
  persisted-session restore keeps existing blocks.
- Warm-pin re-rank: for strategies with preferEarlierSecondaryReset,
  CredentialSelector.resolveOAuth ranks even while the session's automatic
  pin is warm and available (upstream skips ranking inside stickyWarmMs,
  so a busy session never re-ranks). A third automatic-pin eviction policy
  ("soonest reset") evicts the pin only when the best-ranked usable
  sibling ahead of it resets more than SECONDARY_RESET_TIE_TOLERANCE_MS
  earlier (both resets known) — drain/usage differences alone never cost
  the warm prompt cache; a pin that ranks blocked is already dropped by
  upstream. Explicit user pins are exempt.

Rebase notes (17.2.14 -> 18.0.11): upstream added
`pinSessionOAuthAccount` (used by `/session pin` and the
credential-pin session-restore path), absorbing this patch's former
`pinSessionCredential` API. The pin part of this patch is now just the
block-clearing fold into that upstream method, gated to fresh manual
pins. Upstream also added the `usageMeasured` comparator step; the
soonest-reset preference still ranks above it.

Rebased 18.2.10 -> 18.6.0: upstream split the monolithic auth-storage.ts
into auth/* modules behind namespaced APIs (keys.get, oauth.identity,
sessions.pin, limits.markReached, credentials.set/reload). Ranking moved
to the pure auth/rank.ts, selection to auth/select.ts, pins to
auth/affinity.ts. Upstream also added the allowanceSpent / inReserve
comparator steps (above hasPriorityBoost, so above the soonest-reset step)
and an `explicit` flag on session pins (set by the user-facing pin API,
persisted, never evicted by ranking or reserve) with an
automaticPinWouldBeEvicted hook. That `explicit` flag absorbs this patch's
process-local #manualSessionPins map, which is dropped; the warm-pin
`warmPinnedIndex` re-order is re-cut as a soonest-reset eviction policy
inside upstream's automaticPinWouldBeEvicted (checked before and after
OAuth preflight). Block clearing moved into SessionAffinity.pin via an
injected CredentialBlocks. Tests moved to the namespaced API; the
weekly-reset test now uses a temp SqliteAuthCredentialStore instead of a
hand-rolled store (the store interface grew substantially).

